# Paths graphify must not ingest into graphify-out/graph.json.
#
# This file affects ANALYSIS ONLY. graphify-out/ is gitignored and nothing at
# runtime reads it, so excluding a path here cannot change what ships or how
# anything behaves — the files stay on disk and stay tracked.
#
# atlas-three.bundle.js is the vendored, minified, esbuild-generated three.js
# bundle (rebuild: `npm run build:comfy-three` in ui/). It is the frontend's
# ONLY three.js source — atlas_blockout.js imports it directly and there is no
# CDN fallback — so it must remain on disk and in git. But as GRAPH input it
# was pure noise: 950 nodes (15.8% of the graph) and a 947-edge god node, 7.5x
# the next highest, whose "community" was minified internals like a0()/Bc().
#
# Dropping it removed 950 nodes and 2582 edges while EVERY real Atlas node kept
# its exact degree (AtlasIntrinsics 125, AtlasExtrinsics 121, LatentCamera 116,
# unchanged) — proof it was a self-contained island contributing nothing to the
# code graph.
#
# NOTE: `graphify update` fail-closes when an ignore rule newly excludes a file
# that still exists on disk — it KEEPS the old nodes and warns rather than
# silently dropping them. Purge with a full re-extraction:
#     graphify update . --force
atlas_camera/comfy/web/lib/
*.bundle.js
